  "features": [
    "Protected HTTPS ALPN callback bridge supplies SNI and offered protocols, selects an actually offered protocol, and installs selectors on default and registered SNI contexts.",
    "Valid trusted repeated TLS handshakes and HTTP requests verify arguments and selected HTTP/1.1; the valid selection subset also passes the Node reference control."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Accepted-TLSSocket callback receiver compatibility is incomplete; user callback currently receives undefined as receiver. #875 remains open.",
    "Exact constructor validation timing, callback error/shutdown/reentrancy and reload/reconfiguration behavior, encoding and wider platform coverage remain open.",
    "The initial host-memory stop, disk refusal, terminal cache cleanup, portability/validation/receiver control failures are retained. Incorrect server-receiver expectation was removed; receiver compatibility is not counted as passing.",
    "The unchanged seven-file scope retains #874: 60 passes plus three process checks and one registered failure/failed file. It is not green.",
    "Previously excluded constructor/Deno regression files were not rerun and remain unverified. Full suite, #872 and Release/ASAN/all-platform coverage remain open under #66."
  ],
